{"id": "S123", "claim_en": "On the night of 7/8 November 1942 no fewer than 650 aircraft were parked along both sides of the North Front runway for Operation Torch.", "nguon": "Gibraltar Parliament — Notice of Motion (Chief Minister), Freedom of the City for RAF Gibraltar, 17 May 2018", "trich_nguyen_van": "the night of 7/8 November 1942 when no fewer than 650 aircraft of many types were parked along both sides of the runway in readiness for operation TORCH, the Anglo-American invasion of North Africa.", "as_of": "2026-10-17 (ngày đọc)", "phia": "Anh", "status": "XÁC MINH", "ghi_chu": "Dùng cho cảnh 3D 'đường băng chật máy bay'. HMGoG 199/2018 có cùng câu + 'Churchill called it, ‘Gibraltar’s greatest contribution to the War.’' (lời Churchill chưa đối chiếu hồi ký gốc)."}
{"id": "T003", "claim_en": "On 17 July 1704 (O.S.), with the fleet off Tetuan on the African shore, Rooke held a council of war on the Royal Catherine that decided on a sudden attack on Gibraltar; the fleet then crossed the Strait and anchored in the bay (S012).", "nguon": "Capt. Frederick Sayer, The History of Gibraltar (London, 1862)", "trich_nguyen_van": "the admiral, on the 17th July, when within a few leagues of Tetuan, hove to the squadron and called a Council of War on board the flag-ship", "as_of": "đọc 2026-10-17", "phia": "Anh + TBN", "status": "XÁC MINH", "nhay_cam": "THẤP", "ghi_chu": "Bốn nguồn (2 Anh, 2 TBN) khớp. Điểm \"off Tetuan\" = ngoài khơi Martil (cảng của Tétouan), `approx: true`.", "nguon_doi_chieu": [{"nguon": "Francisco María Montero, Historia de Gibraltar y de su campo (Cádiz, 1860)", "trich_nguyen_van": "Estando, pues, la -escuadra á la vista de las costas de Tetuan se celebró un consejo de guerra á bordo de la Real Catalina"}, {"nguon": "W. Laird Clowes et al., The Royal Navy: A History, vol. II (London, 1898)", "trich_nguyen_van": "delayed the fleet, which, by July 17th, had not advanced eastward of Tetuan."}, {"nguon": "Cesáreo Fernández Duro, Armada española desde la unión de los reinos de Castilla y de Aragón, tomo VI (Madrid, 1900)", "trich_nguyen_van": "hechos los preparativos en el fondeadero de Tetuán, pusiéronse á la vela para atravesar el Estrecho"}]}
{"id": "T004", "claim_en": "The war of 1704 pitted the Grand Alliance — England, the Emperor (Austria) and the Dutch Republic — against France and the Spain of Philip V.", "nguon": "Capt. Frederick Sayer, The History of Gibraltar (London, 1862)", "trich_nguyen_van": "was followed by the conclusion of the Grand Alliance, signed on September 7th, between England, the Emperor, and the Dutch. The alliance against Erance and Spain had scarcely been entered into when William III. died", "as_of": "đọc 2026-10-17", "phia": "Anh + TBN", "status": "XÁC MINH", "nhay_cam": "TRUNG BÌNH — chú giải phe: không gọi một bên là \"Spain\" chung chung; dùng \"Spain (Philip V)\" và \"Grand Alliance\".", "ghi_chu": "Đại Liên minh ký 7/9/1701 (Sayer). Fernández Duro gọi phe này là \"los aliados contra la casa de Borbón\" (đúng cách nhìn TBN). Gibraltar bị chiếm nhân danh \"Charles III\" (S012/S017) — chú giải SM1 phải giữ sắc thái này.", "nguon_doi_chieu": [{"nguon": "Lord Mahon [P. H. Stanhope], History of the War of the Succession in Spain (London, 1836)", "trich_nguyen_van": "the basis of the “ Grand Alliance” between Eng- land, Austria, and the States General."}, {"nguon": "Cesáreo Fernández Duro, Armada española desde la unión de los reinos de Castilla y de Aragón, tomo VI (Madrid, 1900)", "trich_nguyen_van": "Su defección alegró á los aliados contra la casa de Borbón"}]}
{"id": "T006", "claim_en": "From July 1779 the Spanish blockade squadron under Admiral Antonio Barceló was based at the anchorage off Algeciras, across the bay from Gibraltar; its aim was to cut the supplies reaching the Rock from the African shore.", "nguon": "John Drinkwater, A History of the Siege of Gibraltar 1779–1783, new ed. (London: John Murray, 1905; text of 1785)", "trich_nguyen_van": "they anchored in the bay, off Algeziras, and being judiciously arranged, and keeping a vigilant lookout, the garrison became closely blockaded.", "as_of": "đọc 2026-10-17", "phia": "Anh + TBN", "status": "XÁC MINH", "nhay_cam": "THẤP", "ghi_chu": "Căn cứ = Algeciras (cả hai phía). Barceló cũng dùng Ceuta (Drinkwater) → vòng phong toả vẽ bao cả Ceuta–Algeciras, nét đứt, không vẽ đường tàu cụ thể.", "nguon_doi_chieu": [{"nguon": "John Drinkwater, A History of the Siege of Gibraltar 1779–1783, new ed. (London: John Murray, 1905; text of 1785)", "trich_nguyen_van": "Admiral Barcelo returned from Ceuta to his old anchorage off Algeziras, and the port again became closely blockaded."}, {"nguon": "Francisco María Montero, Historia de Gibraltar y de su campo (Cádiz, 1860)", "trich_nguyen_van": "Mandaba las fuerzas sutiles marítimas Don Antonio Barceló, general acreditado y aptísimo para este intere- sante servicio del que dependía casi el éxito del bloqueo, encaminado principalmente á privar a la plaza de los vi- veres que le llegaban de las costas de África"}, {"nguon": "Robert Beatson, Naval and Military Memoirs of Great Britain, from 1727 to 1783, vol. V (London, 1804)", "trich_nguyen_van": "retired to Algefiras, where Don Antonio Barcelo, with his line of battle {hips and frigates, hauled as clofe to the fhore"}]}
{"id": "T007", "claim_en": "Spanish lookouts and gunboats were stationed at Cabrita Point (Punta Carnero), the western horn of the bay, to signal and intercept ships entering from the Strait.", "nguon": "John Drinkwater, A History of the Siege of Gibraltar 1779–1783, new ed. (London: John Murray, 1905; text of 1785)", "trich_nguyen_van": "The usual signal for seeing an enemy was made by the Spaniards at Cabrita Point", "as_of": "đọc 2026-10-17", "phia": "Anh + TBN", "status": "XÁC MINH", "nhay_cam": "THẤP", "ghi_chu": "Vị trí tuần tra cố định có nguồn: Punta Carnero/Cabrita Point (1779–82). Không có nguồn cho \"đường tuần tra\" ngoài eo → không vẽ.", "nguon_doi_chieu": [{"nguon": "Francisco María Montero, Historia de Gibraltar y de su campo (Cádiz, 1860)", "trich_nguyen_van": "Cuando esta dobló la punta de Carnero (de cabrita la llaman loa in- gleses) salieron á impedirle el paso quince lanchas ca- ñoneras"}, {"nguon": "Cesáreo Fernández Duro, Armada española desde la unión de los reinos de Castilla y de Aragón, tomo VII (Madrid, 1901)", "trich_nguyen_van": "las cañoneras de Barceló, situadas sobre Punta Carnero"}]}
{"id": "T009", "claim_en": "Rodney's relief fleet put to sea from England on 27 December 1779.", "nguon": "Robert Beatson, Naval and Military Memoirs of Great Britain, from 1727 to 1783, vol. V (London, 1804)", "trich_nguyen_van": "On the 27th of December, 1779, Sir George Rodney put to fea, with twenty fail of the line and nine fri- gates", "as_of": "đọc 2026-10-17", "phia": "Anh + TBN", "status": "XÁC MINH", "nhay_cam": "THẤP", "ghi_chu": "Cảng đi KHÔNG có nguồn nêu thẳng (Drinkwater chỉ ngầm: tàu than \"too late … to join at Spithead\"; Montero viết \"Entrado el de 1780 salió de Londres\" — sai rõ về ngày, coi là ngoại lệ). → Tuyến Rodney vẽ `vao_tu_mep: true`, nhãn \"from England\". Số tàu lệch (20–22 chiến tuyến) → không nói.", "nguon_doi_chieu": [{"nguon": "Cesáreo Fernández Duro, Armada española desde la unión de los reinos de Castilla y de Aragón, tomo VII (Madrid, 1901)", "trich_nguyen_van": "Rodney se hizo á la mar el 27 de Diciembre, escoltando con 22 navios de línea y 10 fragatas el convoy de 200 velas"}, {"nguon": "John Drinkwater, A History of the Siege of Gibraltar 1779–1783, new ed. (London: John Murray, 1905; text of 1785)", "trich_nguyen_van": "she was one of a large convoy which had sailed the latter end of the preceding month for our relief"}]}
{"id": "T013", "claim_en": "Darby's relief fleet sailed in March 1781 — 13 March from St Helens/Spithead by the British count; the Spanish naval historian puts the sailing six days after 22 March.", "nguon": "Robert Beatson, Naval and Military Memoirs of Great Britain, from 1727 to 1783, vol. V (London, 1804)", "trich_nguyen_van": "On the 1 3th of March, Vice- Admiral Darby, with the fleet and the great convoys under his efcort, put to fea from St. Helen's.", "as_of": "đọc 2026-10-17", "phia": "Anh + TBN", "status": "MÂU THUẪN", "nhay_cam": "THẤP", "ghi_chu": "Ba nguồn Anh: 13/3 (St Helens/Spithead) — Clowes dẫn Beatson ở đoạn này, không hẳn độc lập. Fernández Duro: ~28/3 (có thể là ngày rời Cork). Drinkwater: tàu cutter rời Plymouth ~5/3 đã thấy hạm đội \"at anchor in Torbay\" → thêm một chặng dừng không khớp lịch → không vẽ Torbay. Cảng đi Spithead/St Helens có 3 nguồn Anh → vẽ được; bộ đếm SM2 ghi \"Mar 1781\", không ghi ngày.", "nguon_doi_chieu": [{"nguon": "W. Laird Clowes et al., The Royal Navy: A History, vol. III (London, 1898; ch. \"Major Operations 1762–1783\" by A. T. Mahan)", "trich_nguyen_van": "Admiral George Darby, sailed from St. Helen's on the 13th of INIarch, 1781, with a large convoy."}, {"nguon": "Isaac Schomberg, Naval Chronology, vol. II (London, 1802)", "trich_nguyen_van": "On the 13th of March, Vice-Admiral Darby failed from Spithead with the channel fleet"}, {"nguon": "Cesáreo Fernández Duro, Armada española desde la unión de los reinos de Castilla y de Aragón, tomo VII (Madrid, 1901)", "trich_nguyen_van": "Con rumbo á las Occidentales partió la armada francesa el 22 de Marzo de 1781, y con ello desaparecía uno de los cuidados de los britanos; zarparon ellos con 400 velas seis días después"}]}
{"id": "T015", "claim_en": "Howe's relief expedition sailed from Spithead on 11 September 1782.", "nguon": "W. Laird Clowes et al., The Royal Navy: A History, vol. III (London, 1898; ch. \"Major Operations 1762–1783\" by A. T. Mahan)", "trich_nguyen_van": "On the 11th of September the expedition started, 183 sail in all; thirty-four being ships of the line", "as_of": "đọc 2026-10-17", "phia": "Anh", "status": "XÁC MINH", "nhay_cam": "THẤP", "ghi_chu": "Schomberg OCR vỡ ngày (\"r1ith\") → trích hai mảnh; Clowes cho ngày 11/9. Không có nguồn TBN cho ngày đi (Fernández Duro chỉ nói \"procedían de Occidente\").", "nguon_doi_chieu": [{"nguon": "Isaac Schomberg, Naval Chronology, vol. II (London, 1802)", "trich_nguyen_van": "Admiral Lord Howe failed"}, {"nguon": "Isaac Schomberg, Naval Chronology, vol. II (London, 1802)", "trich_nguyen_van": "from Spithead with a powerful fleet for the"}, {"nguon": "W. Laird Clowes et al., The Royal Navy: A History, vol. III (London, 1898; ch. \"Major Operations 1762–1783\" by A. T. Mahan)", "trich_nguyen_van": "it was determined to concentrate the whole Channel Fleet at Spithead, where also the transports and sup[)ly-ships were directed to rendez- vous."}]}
{"id": "T018", "claim_en": "The combined French–Spanish fleet came in through the Strait from the west on the morning of 12 September 1782 and by afternoon lay at anchor between the Orange Grove and Algeciras — about fifty ships of the line by the Spanish count, 47 by the British.", "nguon": "John Drinkwater, A History of the Siege of Gibraltar 1779–1783, new ed. (London: John Murray, 1905; text of 1785)", "trich_nguyen_van": "that a large fleet had appeared in the Straits from the westward.", "as_of": "đọc 2026-10-17", "phia": "Anh + TBN", "status": "XÁC MINH", "nhay_cam": "THẤP", "ghi_chu": "Hướng đến: \"from the westward\" (Drinkwater) → mũi tên vào từ cửa tây eo biển. Số tàu: 47 (Drinkwater) ↔ 50 (Fernández Duro, gồm tàu đã ở Algeciras).", "nguon_doi_chieu": [{"nguon": "John Drinkwater, A History of the Siege of Gibraltar 1779–1783, new ed. (London: John Murray, 1905; text of 1785)", "trich_nguyen_van": "In the afternoon, they were all at anchor in the bay between the Orange Grove and Algeziras."}, {"nguon": "Cesáreo Fernández Duro, Armada española desde la unión de los reinos de Castilla y de Aragón, tomo VII (Madrid, 1901)", "trich_nguyen_van": "hasta el 12 no entró en la bahía la armada, alegrando la vista los 50 navios que se juntaron en Algeciras"}]}
{"id": "T021", "claim_en": "On 12 June 1940, two days after Italy entered the war, Franco's government declared Spain \"non-belligerent\" in place of neutral; the decree appeared in the Boletín Oficial on 13 June.", "nguon": "FRUS 1940, vol. II, doc. 920 — Weddell (Madrid) to Secretary of State, 13 June 1940 (dịch sắc lệnh TBN ngày 12/6/1940)", "trich_nguyen_van": "The hostilities having extended to the Mediterranean by the entrance of Italy into war against France and England the Government has decided upon the non-belligerency of Spain in the conflict. Done in the Pardo the 12th of June, 1940.", "as_of": "đọc 2026-10-17", "phia": "Mỹ dẫn văn bản TBN + Anh", "status": "XÁC MINH", "nhay_cam": "TRUNG BÌNH — gọi đúng \"non-belligerent\", không gọi \"Axis ally\".", "ghi_chu": "Văn bản TBN gốc (BOE 13/6/1940) chưa tải được: bộ tìm Gazeta của BOE không nhận tham số qua curl (thử 2 lần, dừng theo BAI-HOC #12). FRUS dịch nguyên văn sắc lệnh. Nhãn bản đồ 1941: \"Spain (non-belligerent)\".", "nguon_doi_chieu": [{"nguon": "UK Hansard, Commons, \"War Situation\", 20 August 1940 — Mr Cocks (Broxtowe)", "trich_nguyen_van": "Spain at present under Nazi influence has ceased to be neutral and has become non-belligerent"}, {"nguon": "FRUS 1940, vol. II, doc. 919 — Weddell (Madrid) to Secretary of State, 12 June 1940", "trich_nguyen_van": "this might in the first phase at least, be manifest in an attitude of “non-belligerency” in place of the present “neutrality”"}]}
{"id": "T022", "claim_en": "On 14 June 1940 Spanish-commanded Moroccan (Khalifan) troops occupied the Tangier international zone, officially \"provisionally\" and in the Sultan's name; on 3 November 1940 the Spanish commander took over the zone's administration as Governor.", "nguon": "UK Hansard, Commons, \"Tangier International Zone\", 19 June 1940 — R. A. Butler (Under-Secretary, Foreign Office)", "trich_nguyen_van": "On 14th June, the Spanish High Commissioner at Tetuan notified the French Consul-General that, in agreement with the French Government, the Spanish Government intended to occupy Tangier at once.", "as_of": "đọc 2026-10-17", "phia": "Anh + TBN (qua FRUS)", "status": "XÁC MINH", "nhay_cam": "TRUNG BÌNH — \"occupied\" là chữ của cả Anh lẫn văn bản TBN; không nói \"annexed\".", "ghi_chu": "Bản đồ 1941: Tangier đổi từ \"International Zone\" (Cliopatria) sang \"Spanish-occupied (from June 1940)\" — tô màu TBN có gạch, nhãn chữ. Thời điểm kết thúc 1945 KHÔNG có claim → không ghi.", "nguon_doi_chieu": [{"nguon": "FRUS 1940, vol. III, doc. 712 — Weddell (Madrid) to Secretary of State, 14 June 1940 (dịch công hàm của Bộ Ngoại giao TBN)", "trich_nguyen_van": "the High Commissioner of Tetuan was authorized to order Moorish [ Khalifan ] 16c troops, in the name of the Sultan, to occupy Tangier with that view. Said forces have orders to enter the Tangier Zone this morning."}, {"nguon": "UK Hansard, Commons, \"Tangier\", 13 November 1940 — R. A. Butler", "trich_nguyen_van": "On 3rd November the Officer Commanding the Spanish troops in Tangier published a notice stating that by reason of the present situation the Committee of Control, the Legislative Assembly, and the Mixed Bureau of Information would cease to function"}]}
{"id": "T023", "claim_en": "On 8 November 1942 Allied forces landed in French North Africa — at and around Casablanca (French Morocco), Oran and Algiers (Algeria).", "nguon": "UK Hansard, Lords, Address in Reply, 11 November 1942 — Viscount Cranborne (Secretary of State for the Colonies)", "trich_nguyen_van": "The Allied landings had been successfully effected, and effected with no very substantial losses, at Casablanca in French Morocco, at Oran, which is now in Allied hands, and at Algiers", "as_of": "đọc 2026-10-17", "phia": "Anh + Mỹ", "status": "XÁC MINH", "nhay_cam": "THẤP", "ghi_chu": "Bãi đổ bộ chi tiết (Safi, Fedala, Mehdia; Arzew, Les Andalouses; Castiglione, Sidi Ferruch, Surcouf) có trong Howe 1957 nhưng chưa có nguồn thứ hai từng bãi → SM3 chỉ vẽ ba KHU (Casablanca, Oran, Algiers), mũi tên vào bờ `approx: true`.", "nguon_doi_chieu": [{"nguon": "George F. Howe, Northwest Africa (CMH, 1957), ch. XIII \"The Occupation of Algiers\"", "trich_nguyen_van": "Landings at Algiers 8 November 1942"}, {"nguon": "George F. Howe, Northwest Africa (CMH, 1957), ch. XI \"The First Day's Operations Against Oran\"", "trich_nguyen_van": "Operation RESERVIST was instead allowed to begin at 0245, 8 November"}]}
{"id": "T024", "claim_en": "Gibraltar was the command post and air base for Torch: Eisenhower and his staff flew in on 5–6 November 1942 and set up an advanced command post inside the Rock, and the first Twelfth Air Force Spitfires flew from Gibraltar to Tafaraoui (Oran) on 8 November.", "nguon": "George F. Howe, Northwest Africa: Seizing the Initiative in the West (US Army in WWII, CMH, 1957), ch. IV (HyperWar transcription)", "trich_nguyen_van": "Deep within the Rock, in damp and limited quarters excavated during the previous year, General Eisenhower, Commander in Chief, Allied Force, and his principal staff, who flew from the United Kingdom to Gibraltar on 5 and 6 November in B-17's, set up an advanced command post.", "as_of": "đọc 2026-10-17", "phia": "Mỹ + Gibraltar (S122, S123)", "status": "XÁC MINH", "nhay_cam": "THẤP", "ghi_chu": "Đối chiếu Gibraltar: HMGoG 838/2022 (= S122, độc lập với Howe) + S123 (Nghị viện Gibraltar: 650 máy bay đỗ dọc đường băng đêm 7/8/11/1942). Chuyến bay Gibraltar → Tafaraoui chỉ Howe nêu → mũi tên KHÔNG (air) `approx: true`, nhãn \"Spitfires to Oran, 8 Nov\".", "nguon_doi_chieu": [{"nguon": "HM Government of Gibraltar, Press Release 838/2022 (9 Nov 2022) — tải lại 17/10/2026 (SHA khác bản T3b: trang động; câu trích giống S122)", "trich_nguyen_van": "General Eisenhower, who was the overall commander of Operation Torch, based his headquarters in tunnels deep inside the actual Rock itself."}, {"nguon": "George F. Howe, Northwest Africa (CMH, 1957), ch. XI \"The First Day's Operations Against Oran\"", "trich_nguyen_van": "When the first two squadrons of Twelfth Air Force Spitfires from Gibraltar were landed at 1630 at Tafaraoui"}]}
